a16z-anduril-industries:greenhouse:51704.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As Anduril scales its manufacturing footprint to meet the demands of building hyperscale defense systems, our facilities and the systems that run them are mission-critical. We&#39;re looking for a Facilities Engineer to ensure our manufacturing environments operate at peak performance — keeping our production lines, labs, and people running without interruption. In this role, you&#39;ll own the design, programming, and reliability of the Building Automation Systems that control everything from environmental conditions to building infrastructure across our advanced manufacturing facilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer, troubleshoot, and maintain Building Automation Systems, including hardware, servers, software, and networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose and resolve environmental control issues — temperature, humidity, pressure, airflow, noise, and indoor air quality — and implement long-term solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure, program, calibrate, and test controllers and sensors for integration into BAS networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and program setpoints and control logic across temperature, humidity, pressure, scheduling, and equipment state&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate failures, determine root causes, and develop corrective actions and workarounds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and specify system and equipment improvements as well as preventative maintenance programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead special projects, support commissioning of new assets, and identify opportunities for new technology and system integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure safety, maintainability, reliability, ergonomics, and regulatory compliance across all systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer and stakeholder requirements into design options, documentation, estimates, and contract scopes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other related duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor of Science (or higher) from an accredited program in engineering, computer science, mathematics, physics, chemistry, or another related technical discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience with building electrical and mechanical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a facilities engineering role within a manufacturing or industrial environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience with computerized Building Automation Systems (e.g., Trane, Honeywell, Johnson Controls Metasys)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in the aerospace industry supporting Environmental Controls, Flight Controls, and/or Mechanical/Hydraulic Systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Robotics Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of related work experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience with PLC (programmable logic control) hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience with equipment reliability or machine troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience supporting building lighting controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience supporting building environmental controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience modifying computer programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Bluebeam, AutoCAD, and Revit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$129,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$171,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril&#39;s total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
